	title = {Cloud-{Based} {Architecture} and {Algorithms} for {Monitoring} and {Control} of an {Automated} {Greenhouse} {Complex}},
	volume = {231},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85120697130&doi=10.1007%2F978-3-030-90321-3_76&partnerID=40&md5=18d3efa87b3075ec5d6e67a3c432ea73},
	doi = {10.1007/978-3-030-90321-3_76},
	abstract = {To grow crops in greenhouse complexes, it is necessary to maintain the microclimatic conditions required for these crops and to monitor them. Automation of these processes is an urgent task, and for its solution it is necessary to use both hardware and software tools. The paper proposes a cloud service architecture for managing automated vertical farms, which allows for reliable two-way data transfer between the greenhouse modules and the operator and can be used for growing crops both in vertical hydroponic farms and in single-level greenhouse complexes. Algorithms are described that make it possible to understand and evaluate the organizing principles of monitoring and control of growing plants. On the basis of the developed architecture, software has been implemented, which has been tested in the tasks of controlling the greenhouse complex and obtaining data on the microclimate. The use of wireless networks, the absence of restrictions on the type and location of modules, duplication of functionality and data replication makes such a system flexible and scalable. © 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.},
