	abstract = {The increasing complexity and operational demands of high voltage systems in modern power grids necessitate advanced maintenance strategies to ensure reliability, safety, and efficiency. Traditional maintenance approaches, often reactive or schedule-based, are proving inadequate for addressing dynamic grid challenges. This paper explores the improvement as well as application of artificial intelligence (AI) tools for predictive maintenance in high voltage systems. By leveraging machine learning algorithms, deep learning models, and innovative statistics analytics, these trappings allow the real-time observing and analysis of equipment health, facilitating early detection of faults and reducing unplanned outages.},
