	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11455668/},
	doi = {10.1109/IDCIoT67589.2026.11455668},
	abstract = {The most prominent understanding of reliability, safety and other, energy storage systems and in particular, electric vehicles and intelligent grids is Battery State of Health (SoH) and State of Charge (SoC) projections. The innovation of hybrid-form poses an opportunity of the serial application of the machine learning and deep learning model in the SOC and SOH estimations. It has been suggested to apply a Linear Regression, XGBoost, Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN), Bidirectional LSTM, and hybrid LSTM-GRU combination because it is hoped that as many of these temporal and nonlinear behavior impacts on battery behavior could be followed. K-Best feature selection is effective in the improvement of extrapolation of a model as the most significant parts of inputs are only stored. In contrast to the current concept of the unexplainability, the explainable AI approaches-SHAP and LIME- are used to explain the decisions of the model and the extent of the impact of the variables used. With real world experimentally weighted battery data, comparative superiority of our method over the traditional methods is exhibited in accuracy and interpretability. These novel capabilities of this paper comprise a hybrid model architecture and interpretable learning pipeline combined with predictive capability and interpretability. It is massive to sustain the innovations of smart battery management system in the future of this framework.},
