	doi = {10.1109/AIITA69518.2026.11567189},
	abstract = {Industrial process equipment is characterized by strong nonlinearity, multivariable coupling, and dynamic uncertainty, posing significant challenges to traditional control methods. To address these issues, this paper proposes an intelligent control and system integration framework based on deep reinforcement learning. A Soft Actor-Critic (SAC) algorithm is adopted and enhanced with safety-constrained reward design to ensure reliable operation under industrial constraints. Additionally, an LSTM-based state encoder is incorporated to capture temporal dependencies and improve control performance in dynamic environments. A digital twin-assisted hybrid learning strategy is further introduced to enable safe and efficient training. The proposed framework integrates control, optimization, and fault diagnosis into a unified closed-loop architecture. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method significantly outperforms conventional PID, MPC, and baseline DRL methods in terms of tracking accuracy, energy efficiency, and safety. These findings highlight its potential for practical industrial applications.},
