	doi = {10.1109/CAI68641.2026.11536542},
	abstract = {This paper presents a vision-oriented systems contribution that advances the integration of V2X-standardized data, distributed Digital Twin (DT) architectures, and emerging Agentic AI concepts to enhance public Transport Signal Priority (TSP) in urban mobility environments. We propose a V2X-ﬁrst Transportation Digital Twin architecture deployed across the cloud–edge continuum, enabling real-time synchronization between physical infrastructure, predictive AI models, and simulation components. The value of this approach is illustrated through preliminary operational evidence, including a real-world deployment of a TSP service along public bus Line 4 in Granada, achieving a promising reduction in transit time, as well as initial LSTM-based experiments for short-term trafﬁc intensity forecasting. Building on these foundations, the paper introduces an early conceptual design of an Agentic Digital Twin for Transportation (AgDTT), outlining how LLM-based Multi-Agent Systems could automate data ingestion, semantic alignment, anomaly detection, and decision-making in future DT ecosystems.},
