	abstract = {Building upon digital twin frameworks for battery monitoring, this paper introduces an adaptive neural network approach for optimizing vehicle start-stop systems. The proposed ML-enhanced framework integrates Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks for State of Health (SOH) prediction with XGBoost-based optimization for start-stop decision making. By leveraging continuous feedback from the digital twin model, the system achieves adaptive learning capabilities that respond to individual driving patterns. Experimental results demonstrate signiﬁcant improvements: SOH prediction accuracy improved to 1.82\% mean absolute error, while battery life extension reached 24.2\%. The system maintains emission reduction beneﬁts above 92.3\% while adapting optimization thresholds based on realworld usage patterns. The edge-deployable solution requires less than 50ms inference time, making it suitable for real-time automotive applications.},
