	doi = {10.1109/IECCT68664.2026.11541742},
	abstract = {Crop production in modern agriculture needs advanced analytical frameworks to balance production with nutrition and guarantee data integrity. But in traditional precision farming the important link between soil health, crop nutrient density and public well-being is frequently overlooked. BioTwin-Agri presents a digital twin architecture secured by blockchain for nutrition-conscious cultivation, to fill this gap. This system combines all the components of an IoT soil sensor to monitor the environment in the satellite with predictive analytics, and uses a virtual simulation that mimics real-life agricultural scenarios. Soil and crop nutrient intensity is found to vary significantly across various farm data sets. The digital twin gave an outstanding prediction accuracy of 94,8\% (R2 = 0,929), showing a high level of congruence between simulated and observed nutritional values. Moreover, blockchain adoption guarantees data transparency without any doubts over transactions, which has a verification reliability of 96\%. These outcomes validate the fact that BioTwin-Agri is a sturdy and secure base for multi-dimensional agricultural analytics, and can shift the focus from just volume to data-driven nutritional optimization.},
