	address = {Dubai, United Arab Emirates},
	title = {Realization of the danger detector within the framework of the digital twin of the vehicle},
	copyright = {https://doi.org/10.15223/policy-029},
	isbn = {979-8-3315-4531-4},
	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11565102/},
	doi = {10.1109/ICIICE69672.2026.11565102},
	abstract = {The article discusses the implementation of a danger recognition module - a danger detector within the framework of a neuromorphic digital twin of a vehicle. The neuromorphic digital twin is a complex intelligent system. A multiagent approach is usually used to implement such systems. We can talk about the recognition module as a set of agents that solve the tasks of ensuring the safety of the driver and vehicle. The quality of security is directly related to the depth of predictive analytics and the system's ability to make decisions in real time. Thus, the danger detector is a complex dynamic system. Decision-making support in such a system is carried out using artificial intelligence technologies. The implementation of an automatic danger detector is proposed in the pack. The detector supports the processing of four danger levels: normal movement, increased risk, dangerous situation, critical situation. The detector uses a dataset based on embedded protocols and the CAN protocol due to its high accuracy and direct access to the vehicle's internal telemetry. The initial data for training the model is a set obtained using a diagnostic interface (on-board diagnostics) that reads signals directly from the vehicle's CAN bus (the controller's local network). Unlike approaches based on conventional sensors, which depend on the noise level and device locking, CAN bus data can provide processing of deterministic parameters (throttle position, engine load, etc.). The parameters selected from the telemetry stream are used in the analysis process.: vehicle speed, engine speed, throttle position, steering angle. The results obtained in the work confirm the sufficiency of GAN-telemetry for unambiguous determination of the security status. The ML model shows correct results in real time, and is an alternative to complex systems of nested conditions (if-else rules).},
	language = {en},
