	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11513198/},
	doi = {10.1109/TPEC67884.2026.11513198},
	abstract = {The Digital Twin System's most crucial infrastructure systems undergo a radical transformation with the help of a multimodal language algorithm. A power system model can accurately anticipate future demand increases by leveraging a high-fidelity digital twin of the regional grid, powered by a forecasting framework that uses the Dominated Sorting Optimization Algorithm (DSOA). This study examines energy sources, including solar and coal, and microgrid/DER integration by applying the DSOA to capacity indices over many years. While coal capacity steadily shrinks, dispersed assets and renewables are expected to match the rising demand, according to the report. The digital twin makes projections that align with real and expected shifts in generating portfolios by modeling real-world dispatch, congestion patterns, and resource sufficiency across various technology scenarios. Power grid planners may use DSOA-derived load profiles to inform datadriven decisions towards decarbonization by including them in the twin. This allows for systematic testing of control schemes, resilience measures, and investment alternatives.},
