	doi = {10.1109/ICONIC67661.2026.11517666},
	abstract = {Industry 4.0 has accelerated the development of digital twins for monitoring, modeling, and optimizing industrial processes in real time. Conventional digital twin platforms suffer from two-dimensional dashboards and inadequate visualization interfaces, which hinder natural engagement and situational awareness. The goal of this project is to illustrate and manage continuous manufacturing processes by combining augmented reality, virtual reality, and digital twin technologies. Physical and virtual assets are brought into harmony in the proposed architecture using cloud-edge computing infrastructure, industrial IoT sensors, and real-time data streaming. Augmented reality interfaces provide on-site operators with operational analytics, predictive warnings, and maintenance insights, while virtual reality settings allow for immersive simulation, training, and distant collaboration. With the help of the bidirectional architecture, immersive digital models and equipment can receive input in real-time. Immersive environments are ideal for optimizing processes and doing predictive maintenance due to data analytics and machine learning. Evaluation of performance improves operational transparency, operator training, downtime, and decision-making compared to conventional monitoring systems. Scalability, resilience, and human-centric industrial innovation are made possible in smart factories through the use of digital twins and AR/VR, which enhance continuous manufacturing management.},
