	abstract = {Greenhouse agriculture in the Mediterranean faces increasing demand for sustainability and resource ef.ciency. This paper presents the implementation of Controlled Environment Agriculture (CEA) solutions in the Attica region, integrating machine learning (ML) and Digital Twin technologies. An intelligent recommendation system predicts optimal settings for greenhouse microclimates, automatically adjusting components like windows and fans to enhance crop conditions. The system incorporates Random Forest Multioutput models for real-time decision support in energy and climate management. Integration with Digital Twins enables advanced analytics and simulation capabilities. Results indicate signi.cant improvements in energy ef.ciency, resource utilization, and agricultural resilience. Furthermore, the framework supports the development of energy clusters through communication tools and novel business models. This work highlights the potential of ML-driven CEA systems in promoting sustainable agriculture and informed environmental management in the Mediterranean context.},
