	abstract = {The future of military mobility lies in intelligent and self-sustaining vehicular networks capable of autonomous decision making, real-time ¿tness monitoring, and cyber-secure communication. This research introduces a Digital Twin-powered Internet of Military Vehicles (IoMV) framework, transforming traditional military Àeets into highly responsive self-healing systems. By creating virtual replicas of military vehicles, Digital Twins enable continuous real-time diagnostics, predictive analytics, and proactive anomaly detection, minimizing non-battle¿eld casualties and ensuring uncompromised operational readiness. To validate this framework, we deploy SUMO and NS-3 simulations, replicating a dynamic military vehicular ecosystem in Dr. Ambedkar Nagar, Indore, India. Our experiments evaluate key performance metrics, including adaptive response time, predictive maintenance accuracy, reduction of communication latency, and network resilience. The results reveal a 55\% improvement in maintenance e൶ciency, a 40 \% reduction in unexpected failures, and a signi¿cant boost in secure data exchange. This work pioneers an AI-driven and cyber-resilient IoMV architecture, establishing the foundation for next-generation autonomous military logistics, intelligent battle¿eld coordination, and enhancde survivability in hostile environments. As the digital battle¿eld evolves, this research marks a paradigm shift in military vehicular intelligence, where machines no longer just move, but think, predict and protect.},
