	abstract = {Aiming at the core pain points of single data dimension and lagging anomaly detection in building energy consumption monitoring, this paper proposes an intelligent monitoring system. The system realizes multimodal data collection through edge computing nodes and uses an improved variational mode decomposition algorithm to extract multiscale features of non-stationary current signals. The core algorithm layer constructs a hybrid deep learning framework, in which the long short-term memory network (LSTM) captures the time-series dependency of energy consumption, the random forest algorithm processes discrete features such as the start and stop status of equipment, and realizes bimodal feature fusion through the attention mechanism. The system deployment layer adopts the edge-cloud collaborative computing architecture to build a digital twin-driven decision engine, decouple the energy consumption prediction results from the building equipment control logic, and generate a dynamic tuning strategy. Under this system, the building EER improvement rate reaches up to 29.5\%, and the cumulative carbon emission reduction is 17,968kgCO₂, providing an adaptive and evolvable intelligent solution for building energy consumption management.},
