	doi = {10.1109/SISIMPACT67725.2025.11439547},
	abstract = {Aiming at the problem of energy consumption deviating from the design target due to dynamic environmental changes and control strategy lag in the operation of green buildings, this study proposes an intelligent control system based on artificial intelligence. The system first integrates multisource IoT (Internet of Things) sensors and external meteorological and power grid data to achieve panoramic perception; the core adopts the proximal policy optimization (PPO) framework to dynamically optimize energy consumption, indoor comfort and energy cost through autonomous learning; the transfer learning technology is applied, and the lightweight digital twin rehearsal strategy is combined to ensure safety and reliability; finally, the equipment is controlled in real time through edge computing. Experiments show that the system has achieved an average energy consumption reduction of about 12\% in the energy consumption optimization experiment for 30 consecutive days. In the peak load reduction experiment, the maximum load is reduced by 14.88\%; the average response time is shortened to 819.5ms; the fluctuation coefficient is reduced to 0.060. The comprehensive results show that the multi-objective collaborative control system driven by PPO has the advantages of energy saving, high efficiency and stable operation, and can provide intelligent and reliable energy optimization solutions for the operation of real estate green buildings, with good promotion value.},
