	doi = {10.1109/MoSICom67153.2025.11398191},
	abstract = {In order to increase safety, dependability, and efficiency, the oil and gas sector is adopting “Maintenance 5.0” a shift to Internet of Things (IoT)-based smart maintenance. To enable predictive and proactive maintenance of oil and gas operations, this paper offers a thorough proposal for Maintenance 5.0, which combines human expertise with cuttingedge IoT sensors, real-time analytics, and artificial intelligence (AI). We identify a gap in the application of cutting-edge Industry 5.0 concepts of sustainable and human-centered asset management, to oil and gas maintenance in particular. Our proposal is to implement an IoT-enabled smart maintenance architecture that supports maintenance decision-making by utilizing digital twin simulations, edge / cloud data processing pipelines, machine learning models for fault prediction, and continuous sensor monitoring. This strategy can improve the accuracy of forecasting equipment failure by up to 46.8 \% in a case study. The outcomes improve safety and compliance, extend asset life, and save maintenance costs by about 28.02 \%. We discuss how these findings affect oil and gas sustainability and operational efficacy. This study offers insights for researchers and industry experts to rethink maintenance practices using IoT and AI, and it contributes to a futuristic view of Maintenance 5.0 deployment in the oil and gas sector.},
