	abstract = {With the continuous improvement of the intelligence level of the power grid, traditional manual inspection methods are no longer able to meet the high requirements for real-time and precision in modern transmission line operation and maintenance. Therefore, this article proposes a transmission line inspection and status assessment technology system that integrates digital twin and drone technology. This system is based on multi-source perception, constructing a three-dimensional digital mapping model of transmission lines, realizing real-time interconnection of virtual and real data, and combining with improved YOLOv5-Mv3 deep learning algorithm to achieve automatic recognition and state quantification evaluation of fault images. The system architecture includes a physical entity layer, a perceptual transport layer, a digital twin modeling layer, and a visual decision layer, forming a "perception cognition decision" closed-loop mechanism. The experiment was conducted on a 220kV line, and the verification results showed that the average accuracy of system defect recognition reached 86.2\%, the deviation between health assessment and manual scoring did not exceed ± 0.09, the inspection cycle was shortened by 65\%, and the operation and maintenance efficiency and intelligence level were significantly improved. This system has good engineering practicality and provides effective support for the digital transformation of the power grid.},
