	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11153000/},
	doi = {10.1109/INFOCOMWKSHPS65812.2025.11153000},
	abstract = {In this paper, we propose a semantic-twin-enabled bifurcated control architecture for multi-unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) tasks in remote areas. To mitigate the effects of interference channels and construct a task-oriented digital twin (DT), we propose the concept of semantic twin (ST), which transmits semantics extracted from perceptual data and optimizes channel utilization. To achieve efﬁcient remote control, we develop a bifurcated control architecture based on ST, in which satellites and the ground control station (GCS) function as edge controllers and the remote controller, respectively. On this basis, we design a ST-enabled model-based ofﬂine reinforcement learning algorithm for lifelong learning. By building a virtual target and reﬁning the weighted sampling, model ensemble and regularization methods, we ensure the reliability of the virtual environment and the efﬁcacy of ofﬂine model training. Finally, we validate this framework by designing a multi-UAV tracking task, and verify the signiﬁcant advantages of the proposed control architecture in scenario reconstruction and decision performance, proving the effectiveness of ST-enabled bifurcated control architecture in remote UAV tasks.},
