	doi = {10.1109/AECTSD65988.2025.11410935},
	abstract = {The development of Digital Twin (DT) technology from descriptive simulation to independent decision-making represents a big leap towards Industry 5.0. In this paper, a Cognitive Digital Twin (CDT) architecture with ReinforcementOptimized Deep Learning (RODL) integration is proposed for intelligent and adaptive control of industrial processes. The architecture combines real-time sensor streams with deep neural representations, where the Deep Q-Learning (DQL) agent is self-tuning the operation parameters like energy usage, equipment dependability and production rate. The MultiObjective Swarm Optimization (MOSO) strategy directs the reinforcement agent to balance performance and sustainability goals optimally. The results demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed framework. Component-wise evaluation shows that pre-processing achieves an RMSE of 0.08 and the cognitive deep learning model predicts with 95.6\% accuracy. The reinforcement learning agent attains an average reward of 0.92 and swarm optimization balances multiple objectives with a fitness score of 0.89. The overall control feedback system achieves a performance score of 0.94. Through cognitive integration, CDT-RODL architecture is a scalable platform for next-generation intelligent manufacturing, energy management. and healthcare automation.},
