	doi = {10.1109/EEEIC/ICPSEurope64998.2025.11169068},
	abstract = {This paper presents an AI-driven digital twin framework for real-time condition monitoring and fault detection of photovoltaic (PV) systems. The proposed approach integrates IoT-based sensor data, physics-informed synthetic fault generation, and interpretable machine learning to detect and diagnose common PV faults, such as partial shading, inverter failures, and panel degradation, with high accuracy. Synthetic faults were modeled using physically inspired equations by altering key parameters like irradiance, voltage, and power output. Data was collected from a real PV setup using Arduino-connected sensors and transmitted in real time to the ThingSpeak IoT platform. A bagged decision tree ensemble model was trained on a combination of real and synthetic data, achieving a cross-validation accuracy of 99.6\%. The proposed framework bridges the gap between data-driven AI and physicsbased modeling in PV monitoring, offering a scalable and explainable solution for smart energy systems.},
