	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11486898/},
	doi = {10.1109/CAC67268.2025.11486898},
	abstract = {In industrial automation, multi-motor collaborative control systems face challenges such as strong model dependency and insufficient real-time performance. This paper proposes a novel Edge Computing-Enhanced Digital Twin with Deep Reinforcement Learning (ECDT+DRL) fusion control framework. Lightweight digital twins deployed on edge nodes enable real-time updates of electromagnetic-mechanical parameters, reducing state estimation complexity to O(1). A hierarchical "local MPC optimization–cloud ADMM coordination" mechanism is established, supported by cloudbased dynamic Bayesian inference. An Actor-Critic DRL agent integrates a 24-dimensional state space and a multi-objective reward function, optimizing PID gains and PWM frequencies via a Hierarchical Attention Network. Experiments on a threePMSM platform show a synchronization error within 0.1° and an adjustment time of 50 ms under 50\% rated torque step disturbance. High-frequency tests reveal a 78\% reduction in steady-state error compared to MPC, and 24.8\%–56.2\% lower MSE in trajectory tracking. The main contributions include: a fused edge-cloud-DRL architecture, real-time lightweight twin modeling, hierarchical optimization coordination, and enhanced performance in high-dynamic environments.},
