	doi = {10.1109/AECSPE66597.2025.00087},
	abstract = {The traditional inspection and maintenance methods are inefficient and subjective, and it is difficult to meet the expanding demand of substation secondary system under the background of smart grid. In this paper, an intelligent analysis and decision support platform integrating multi-source sensor data, machine learning algorithm and digital twin technology is proposed, aiming at realizing realtime perception of multi-physical quantities of connection state, intelligent fault diagnosis based on deep learning, and maintenance decision support combined with risk assessment. The platform adopts a four-layer distributed architecture of "edge-cloud" cooperation, including perception layer, edge layer, platform layer and application layer. Through the research of key technologies such as multi-source data fusion modeling, intelligent fault diagnosis model, decision support based on risk assessment and digital twinning realization, the accuracy of fault diagnosis and the scientificity of operation and maintenance decision-making have been significantly improved. The experimental results show that the platform performs well in composite fault identification, real-time perception, maintenance priority evaluation and robustness under extreme working conditions, which provides strong technical support for monitoring and maintaining the quality of secondary cable connection in substation and helps to improve the operation and maintenance level of substation and the stability of power grid.},
