	abstract = {Traditional concrete testing, reliant on extended curing periods, is costly and yields delayed results, impeding effective quality control. The heterogeneous nature of concrete, driven by site-speciﬁc variations in mix compositions and environmental conditions, creates transferability challenges for datadriven models. To address this, we propose a workﬂow-driven digital twin framework that orchestrates real-time data integration from mixing plants, warehouses, and laboratories, enabling precise, site-speciﬁc concrete property prediction through tailored HHO-ANFIS models. A case study from the Hanjiang-To-Weihe River Valley Water Diversion Project validates the framework’s effectiveness, demonstrating superior prediction accuracy and adaptability to local conditions while optimizing mix designs. This scalable, automated solution enhances quality control and advances industrial automation in concrete production.},
