	doi = {10.1109/STPEC66316.2025.11490532},
	abstract = {This study presents a data-driven black-box Digital Twin (DT) framework for real-time diagnosis and predictive failure analysis of power converters. While designed to be applicable to any unknown converter, the framework is demonstrated on a solar photovoltaic (SPV)-powered boost converter with resistive load. Leveraging a Multi-Task Temporal Convolutional Network (MT-TCN), the proposed DT simultaneously performs health condition estimation and Remaining Useful Life (RUL) prediction by learning directly from multidimensional operational datasets. Unlike conventional physics-based approaches, the data-driven model inherently adapts to nonlinear degradation dynamics and varying solar conditions, ensuring robust performance across diverse scenarios. A high-fidelity experimental setup integrated with the OPAL-RT platform is used for dataset generation and real-time validation. Results confirm that the developed DT achieves more than 96\% accuracy, with mean absolute error consistently below 2.5\%. These outcomes highlight its strong potential for reliable degradation monitoring and nextgeneration DT deployment in smart energy infrastructure.},
