	abstract = {The rapid expansion in Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) applications has created the necessity for simulation frameworks that are capable of handling real-time analytics and predictive maintenance. In this paper, authors explain a technique for simulating real-time sensor readings from cement plant machinery using the OPC Uniﬁed Architecture (OPCUA) along with modern-day data ingestion tools. Multiparameter sensor data streams are fed into and processed by an integrated pipeline of Telegraf, InﬂuxDB, and machine learning models for condition monitoring with anomaly detection and maintenance forecasting. Connecting industrial communication standards to AI-based analytics, the system provides an experimentally controlled environment where digital twin concepts are validated and predictive maintenance strategies are tried. Outcomes validate interoperability, ﬁdelity of data, and scalability to support deployment of robust predictive solutions into advanced manufacturing environments.},
