	doi = {10.1109/TEMSMET65536.2025.11467356},
	abstract = {This paper presents a cloud-integrated digital twin architecture for real-time battery monitoring and intelligent State of Charge (SOC) prediction in electric vehicle (EV) systems. The system leverages a lightweight Internet of Things (IoT) framework based on an ESP32 microcontroller interfaced with voltage, current, temperature, and GPS sensors. Sensor data is transmitted to a Firebase Realtime Database using HTTPS protocols, enabling seamless cloud synchronization and remote access. A hybrid SOC estimation model combining a Kalman Filter and Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) is employed to enhance prediction accuracy, achieving a mean absolute error of 2.6\%. A React-based dashboard visualizes real-time parameters, SOC trends, location, and system alerts for threshold violations. The proposed system offers a scalable, low-cost solution for EV battery management, predictive maintenance, and digital twin modeling.},
