	doi = {10.1109/CSITSS67709.2025.11295713},
	abstract = {This paper reviews recent advances (2022–2025) in digital twin–driven predictive maintenance (PdM) for belt-driven conveyors, highlighting IoTenabled sensor integration, virtual fault simulation, and machine learning methods for anomaly detection and remaining useful life (RUL) prediction. It proposes a smart system using an ARM-Linux edge device (e.g., Raspberry Pi 4) to collect and preprocess data from seven sensors, feeding ML models for real-time diagnostics. A digital twin simulates failure scenarios, and the ML pipeline combines autoencoders and RUL regression. Deployment and evaluation metrics are discussed, with code examples provided.},
