	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11454954/},
	doi = {10.1109/PEEEC67807.2025.00027},
	abstract = {The proposed research is expected to fill in the existing studies in the area of prefabricated construction optimization, namely, the fragmentation of the model, the presence of a single objective, and the lack of integration with real-world applications, by building an overall intelligent decision-support system that unites digital twin technology and multi-objective optimization. The study is aimed at creating a single approach to decision-making incorporating data-driven LCA based carbon footprint prediction, optimization with the use of machine learning, and 3D representation. The article combines the XGBoost-predicted carbon emissions model and the NSGA-II algorithm, and the outcomes indicate that it provides a collaborative optimization model that acts as a unifier of the cost, time, and environmental goals. Moreover, digital twin platform with support by Unity and Model Predictive Control (MPC) allows dynamic rolling optimization, which supports flexible and transparent decision-making in complex tasks via planning of lifting sequences and support system design. The framework will improve construction transparency, flexibility, and uncertainty resiliency through 3D visualisation and real-time interaction of data.},
