	abstract = {य़is study introduces a digital-twin-driven vision-based robotic pick-and-place system tailored for high-mix, low-volume production scenarios. By leveraging sub-millimeter precision vision and millisecond-level synchronization with a digital twin (DT), the system achieves high accuracy and real-time performance. Key innovations include an edge-template coupled pose estimation algorithm and an Open Platform Communications (OPC) Data Access (DA)-based data loop ensuring {\textless}100 ms latency. य़e lightweight DT in NX/Process Simulate enables online monitoring and predictive maintenance. Continuous operation tests validate a 99.4\% grasp success rate and ±0.2° joint-angle synchronization accuracy. य़e system exhibits strong robustness against illumination changes and rapid recon੗guration ability. Future work will focus on further reducing communication latency using OPC Uni੗ed Architecture (UA)-PubSub and Time-Sensitive Networking (TSN), and enhancing real-time adaptability through deep reinforcement learning.},
