	doi = {10.1145/3773365.3773489},
	abstract = {Under the “Dual Carbon” goals, public buildings represent a major sector for energy consumption and carbon emissions in the construction industry, making energy-eਖ਼cient and low-carbon development of public buildings a critical priority for China’s lowcarbon urban development objectives. To address challenges such as the lack of real-time user behavior interaction, prolonged operation of HVAC and lighting systems in unoccupied spaces, and inappropriate temperature se॒ings in public buildings. य़is study proposes an AI-based intelligent edge autonomous control system for smart public buildings.य़is system, designed around user behavior, integrates arti੗cial intelligence, machine learning, the Internet of य़ings (IoT), big data, cloud computing, and digital twin technologies to establish a real-time, self-updating building model with automated control. It could ensure compatibility between public building environments and user scenarios while delivering an e੖ective solution for energy conservation and carbon reduction.य़e system employs millimeter-wave radar sensors to autonomously detect and assess occupancy, temperature, humidity, illuminance, and air quality within public building spaces. Additionally, it utilizes AI-powered edge computing to perform 24/7 automated decision-making for oਖ਼ces, meeting rooms, and open areas based on zonal management objectives and user behavior pa॒erns, issuing real-time control commands to terminal devices to achieve energy and emission reductions. A pilot implementation in an oਖ਼ce building validated the system’s feasibility, with energy performance data demonstrating that the intelligent edge autonomous control system enables zonal management, e੖ectively resolving delays in environmental energy management and minimizing energy waste. य़e system reduces operational energy consumption and carbon emissions by over 25\%, con੗rming its signi੗cant impact on public building sustainability.},
